1
00:00:12,910 --> 00:00:14,430
This rain isn't going
to stop anytime soon.

2
00:00:14,510 --> 00:00:15,400
Let's head back first.

3
00:00:15,400 --> 00:00:17,070
We'll come back tomorrow
and clear that area.

4
00:00:17,070 --> 00:00:18,390
What about our equipment?

5
00:00:19,390 --> 00:00:20,600
Why don't you leave it here?

6
00:00:20,920 --> 00:00:23,390
This looks like an old electrical box.

7
00:00:24,870 --> 00:00:26,600
Do you smell something?

8
00:00:27,320 --> 00:00:27,870
A smell?

9
00:00:30,280 --> 00:00:31,160
What?

10
00:00:31,160 --> 00:00:31,830
What smell?

11
00:00:31,830 --> 00:00:32,520
What could there be?

12
00:00:32,560 --> 00:00:34,110
Hurry up, put the stuff down
and let's go home.

13
00:00:48,860 --> 00:00:52,860
=Medical Examiner Dr. Qin: Bones of the Past=
=Episode 8=

14
00:00:53,200 --> 00:00:55,030
Liang Chao must have started planning

15
00:00:55,030 --> 00:00:56,240
and carrying out both murders

16
00:00:56,240 --> 00:00:57,600
more than a month before the crimes.

17
00:00:57,600 --> 00:00:59,520
The timing and motive both fit.

18
00:00:59,960 --> 00:01:01,560
Don't you think things
are going a little too smoothly?

19
00:01:01,560 --> 00:01:02,920
Whatever clue we need,

20
00:01:02,920 --> 00:01:04,590
we seem to find it right away.

21
00:01:05,070 --> 00:01:06,680
Our top priority is to find Liang Chao.

22
00:01:06,870 --> 00:01:09,000
Only then can we unravel
this seemingly perfect case.

23
00:01:09,150 --> 00:01:10,000
How about this?

24
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:11,790
Get everyone together for a meeting

25
00:01:12,120 --> 00:01:13,400
and work out a plan to apprehend him.

26
00:01:19,870 --> 00:01:20,680
Zhuang.

27
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:24,070
Something wrong?

28
00:01:25,230 --> 00:01:26,040
No.

29
00:01:27,920 --> 00:01:28,950
Just say it.

30
00:01:29,680 --> 00:01:31,510
If you're having trouble
in your personal life or at home,

31
00:01:31,510 --> 00:01:33,430
the community
and the bureau can both help.

32
00:01:35,400 --> 00:01:36,430
Thank you, Captain Qin.

33
00:01:37,200 --> 00:01:38,230
I'm not having any difficulties.

34
00:01:39,480 --> 00:01:41,590
The bureau and the community
have already treated me very well.

35
00:01:48,560 --> 00:01:49,640
I just wanted to ask

36
00:01:50,480 --> 00:01:52,590
if there's still no news

37
00:01:53,680 --> 00:01:54,920
about my wife, Liu Yan.

38
00:01:57,790 --> 00:01:58,640
Officer.

39
00:01:58,950 --> 00:02:00,120
This... This is my daughter.

40
00:02:00,120 --> 00:02:02,430
She said she'd come home
for dinner yesterday.

41
00:02:02,510 --> 00:02:03,680
(Duty Room)
But she didn't come home.

42
00:02:03,680 --> 00:02:05,430
And I still haven't heard from her.

43
00:02:06,480 --> 00:02:08,680
Sir, don't worry just yet.

44
00:02:08,680 --> 00:02:09,520
Think carefully.

45
00:02:09,870 --> 00:02:11,120
Could she have gone to visit a friend

46
00:02:11,120 --> 00:02:12,470
or a coworker?

47
00:02:12,470 --> 00:02:14,120
Or could something
have delayed her on the way?

48
00:02:14,190 --> 00:02:16,120
No. She's always very punctual.

49
00:02:16,120 --> 00:02:17,560
Even if something came up, she would

50
00:02:17,560 --> 00:02:19,240
call the public phone
at the end of the alley

51
00:02:19,240 --> 00:02:20,280
and ask them to let me know.

52
00:02:20,280 --> 00:02:21,280
She's never

53
00:02:21,280 --> 00:02:22,710
just disappeared without saying a word

54
00:02:22,710 --> 00:02:24,000
like this before.

55
00:02:24,030 --> 00:02:26,680
Sir, don't worry just yet.
Sit down and tell me what happened.

56
00:02:28,520 --> 00:02:31,240
I'd like to get some basic
information about your daughter.

57
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:33,590
Her name, age, and occupation.

58
00:02:33,680 --> 00:02:35,750
My daughter's name is Liu Yan.

59
00:02:35,870 --> 00:02:37,630
Liu as in willow,
Yan as in bright and beautiful.

60
00:02:38,280 --> 00:02:39,150
She's 35.

61
00:02:39,150 --> 00:02:41,710
She's an accountant
at Longfan Urban Construction Group.

62
00:02:41,960 --> 00:02:44,750
Is she married?
Does she have any children?

63
00:02:45,030 --> 00:02:46,680
And how is her relationship
with her husband?

64
00:02:47,560 --> 00:02:48,430
She's married.

65
00:02:49,000 --> 00:02:50,710
They have a daughter.

66
00:02:51,120 --> 00:02:52,030
As for their relationship,

67
00:02:53,680 --> 00:02:54,590
it's all right.

68
00:02:55,030 --> 00:02:55,870
Pretty good.

69
00:02:55,870 --> 00:02:57,470
My daughter is already gone.

70
00:02:57,960 --> 00:02:59,400
Now she's all I have left.

71
00:03:04,360 --> 00:03:05,310
Not yet.

72
00:03:05,590 --> 00:03:06,560
If we hear anything,

73
00:03:07,190 --> 00:03:09,280
I'll let you know right away, okay?

74
00:03:10,430 --> 00:03:11,240
Okay.

75
00:03:12,430 --> 00:03:13,360
Thank you, Captain Qin.

76
00:03:13,360 --> 00:03:14,080
You're welcome.

77
00:03:14,080 --> 00:03:14,590
Thank you.

78
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:15,470
Captain Qin.

79
00:03:16,240 --> 00:03:17,080
Zhao is back.

80
00:03:17,120 --> 00:03:18,240
We can start the meeting.

81
00:03:18,750 --> 00:03:19,870
He's back already?

82
00:03:20,750 --> 00:03:21,710
All right, then.

83
00:03:22,960 --> 00:03:23,800
Let's get ready.

84
00:03:24,520 --> 00:03:25,310
I...

85
00:03:34,310 --> 00:03:36,240
I really feel sorry for Zhuang.

86
00:03:37,150 --> 00:03:38,080
His daughter is gone,

87
00:03:39,190 --> 00:03:40,360
his wife is missing,

88
00:03:41,080 --> 00:03:43,400
and he's been dragged into
this awful fundraising fraud case.

89
00:03:44,430 --> 00:03:47,000
Huo Qicheng
did all those terrible things,

90
00:03:47,710 --> 00:03:49,190
yet we still have
to find his real killer.

91
00:03:49,560 --> 00:03:51,120
What kind of world is this?

92
00:03:51,280 --> 00:03:52,360
Do good people
really get nothing in return?

93
00:03:52,360 --> 00:03:53,560
All right, that's enough.

94
00:03:53,870 --> 00:03:54,840
Listen.

95
00:03:55,560 --> 00:03:57,840
If a good person kills someone,
we still have to arrest them.

96
00:03:58,240 --> 00:03:59,800
If a bad person is dying,
we still have to save them.

97
00:03:59,800 --> 00:04:00,590
Understand?

98
00:04:01,560 --> 00:04:03,840
Stop clinging to me all day long.

99
00:04:10,080 --> 00:04:10,870
Mom.

100
00:04:11,430 --> 00:04:15,800
Dad said that as long
as I turn off my walkie-talkie,

101
00:04:15,910 --> 00:04:19,600
the Mr. Know-It-All will talk through
his walkie-talkie.

102
00:04:20,000 --> 00:04:23,240
I haven't turned on
my walkie-talkie in a long time.

103
00:04:23,240 --> 00:04:26,390
When will the Mr. Know-It-All show up?

104
00:04:26,390 --> 00:04:28,000
Mr. Know-It-All is busy too.

105
00:04:28,120 --> 00:04:29,630
Ming has to be patient.

106
00:04:29,750 --> 00:04:30,560
Son.

107
00:04:30,600 --> 00:04:32,360
Dad, you're back.

108
00:04:32,830 --> 00:04:33,630
You're back.

109
00:04:34,070 --> 00:04:35,000
I made

110
00:04:35,000 --> 00:04:36,510
your favorite braised fish today.

111
00:04:37,040 --> 00:04:37,630
Great.

112
00:04:37,630 --> 00:04:38,430
Dad.

113
00:04:38,750 --> 00:04:42,070
The light on this walkie-talkie
flashed a few times just now,

114
00:04:42,560 --> 00:04:45,630
but I didn't hear
the Mr. Know-It-All's voice.

115
00:04:45,800 --> 00:04:47,920
It's okay. I'll try contacting him.

116
00:04:47,920 --> 00:04:48,630
Okay.

117
00:04:51,830 --> 00:04:52,630
Mom.

118
00:04:53,000 --> 00:04:54,510
I have something for you.

119
00:04:54,510 --> 00:04:55,310
Good boy.

120
00:04:56,000 --> 00:04:58,680
Ming, sorry to keep you waiting.

121
00:04:58,950 --> 00:04:59,870
I'll keep this brief.

122
00:04:59,950 --> 00:05:01,820
We've identified Liang Chao,

123
00:05:01,820 --> 00:05:03,370
the Deputy General Manager
of Longfan Urban Construction Group.

124
00:05:03,830 --> 00:05:05,000
He's a major suspect,

125
00:05:05,360 --> 00:05:06,510
but we haven't found him yet.

126
00:05:06,950 --> 00:05:08,390
Nothing has changed on your end, right?

127
00:05:08,430 --> 00:05:09,240
No.

128
00:05:09,680 --> 00:05:11,720
Dad, go eat.

129
00:05:13,070 --> 00:05:14,070
You rascal.

130
00:05:14,430 --> 00:05:16,070
You and your mom make sure you eat too.

131
00:05:17,870 --> 00:05:18,680
Got it, Dad.

132
00:05:19,310 --> 00:05:20,750
I won't let your wife go hungry.

133
00:05:30,300 --> 00:05:35,180
(Winter 2000)

134
00:05:37,720 --> 00:05:39,560
I know how to do this. Let me.

135
00:05:51,160 --> 00:05:51,950
When you were little,

136
00:05:52,160 --> 00:05:54,310
you always liked helping me
prepare food in the kitchen.

137
00:05:57,160 --> 00:05:58,720
Later, you stopped
letting me into the kitchen.

138
00:05:59,040 --> 00:06:00,120
You were afraid I'd cut myself,

139
00:06:00,870 --> 00:06:01,920
afraid I'd get splattered with hot oil,

140
00:06:02,430 --> 00:06:03,240
afraid...

141
00:06:03,240 --> 00:06:04,240
Afraid you'd get hurt.

142
00:06:34,430 --> 00:06:35,240
Eat.

143
00:06:47,630 --> 00:06:48,430
Qin.

144
00:06:49,390 --> 00:06:50,430
Take a look at this too.

145
00:06:54,160 --> 00:06:54,870
This man

146
00:06:54,870 --> 00:06:57,560
turned up when we
investigated Huo Qicheng's

147
00:06:57,560 --> 00:06:58,750
social connections back then.

148
00:06:58,830 --> 00:06:59,630
Liang Chao.

149
00:07:00,070 --> 00:07:01,960
He was the Deputy General Manager

150
00:07:01,960 --> 00:07:03,000
of Huo Qicheng's
Urban Construction Company.

151
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,120
His right-hand man.

152
00:07:04,360 --> 00:07:05,560
After Huo Qicheng died,

153
00:07:05,560 --> 00:07:07,240
he was one of the biggest beneficiaries.

154
00:07:07,630 --> 00:07:08,630
This is Liang Chao.

155
00:07:10,480 --> 00:07:11,680
Is he mentioned in the case file?

156
00:07:12,360 --> 00:07:13,160
No.

157
00:07:14,270 --> 00:07:16,040
Then why do you sound like
you know him so well?

158
00:07:16,310 --> 00:07:17,120
Section Chief Qin.

159
00:07:17,870 --> 00:07:18,680
What's wrong?

160
00:07:18,680 --> 00:07:20,190
I clearly

161
00:07:20,190 --> 00:07:21,390
organized all the case files

162
00:07:21,390 --> 00:07:22,390
from 1990 for you before.

163
00:07:22,390 --> 00:07:23,950
But I just checked
and found another one.

164
00:07:24,820 --> 00:07:27,900
(Case Name: Mummy in the Rain Case)

165
00:07:32,920 --> 00:07:33,870
You okay, Qin?

166
00:07:34,920 --> 00:07:36,480
An unsolved case scared you that badly?

167
00:07:37,480 --> 00:07:38,750
There's another new case.

168
00:07:40,070 --> 00:07:41,240
Didn't you say

169
00:07:41,390 --> 00:07:43,680
you'd read all the unsolved case files?

170
00:07:44,480 --> 00:07:46,830
I did, but...

171
00:07:47,920 --> 00:07:49,680
You're going to say this one
wasn't there either, right?

172
00:07:53,870 --> 00:07:55,070
Was it supposed to be?

173
00:07:57,160 --> 00:07:58,240
If it wasn't,

174
00:07:58,240 --> 00:08:00,040
why would there be
a record of it in the archives?

175
00:08:00,190 --> 00:08:01,920
It's not like the case just happened.

176
00:08:04,600 --> 00:08:06,560
This case did just happen.

177
00:08:11,750 --> 00:08:12,950
With rain this heavy,

178
00:08:12,950 --> 00:08:14,360
how could there be a mummified body?

179
00:08:15,240 --> 00:08:16,040
Officer.

180
00:08:16,920 --> 00:08:17,720
Tell Captain Wang.

181
00:08:17,720 --> 00:08:19,040
- Got it.
- I'll take a look at the scene first.

182
00:08:20,040 --> 00:08:21,680
Officer, here's what happened.

183
00:08:21,800 --> 00:08:23,190
A few workers

184
00:08:23,190 --> 00:08:24,800
opened the metal box
to put their tools inside

185
00:08:24,800 --> 00:08:25,950
and keep them dry.

186
00:08:28,560 --> 00:08:31,120
We haven't found anything
suspicious nearby so far.

187
00:08:31,480 --> 00:08:32,960
When was this area cleared?

188
00:08:32,960 --> 00:08:34,025
Has the trace evidence team

189
00:08:34,025 --> 00:08:35,100
- collected all the evidence at the scene?
- When exactly was this area cleared?

190
00:08:35,100 --> 00:08:35,930
- Everything's been collected.
- About three months ago.

191
00:08:35,930 --> 00:08:36,630
All right, thanks for your hard work.

192
00:08:36,630 --> 00:08:38,080
This used to be
an old residential neighborhood.

193
00:08:38,120 --> 00:08:39,260
Quite a few people lived here.

194
00:08:39,260 --> 00:08:40,200
Once the land
acquisition order came down,

195
00:08:40,200 --> 00:08:41,720
they all moved out promptly.

196
00:08:42,360 --> 00:08:43,600
All right, thank you.

197
00:08:43,630 --> 00:08:44,790
Go ahead and get back to work.

198
00:08:44,840 --> 00:08:45,630
Will do.

199
00:08:47,440 --> 00:08:48,670
A lot of people lived here.

200
00:08:49,030 --> 00:08:50,240
So there must have
been a lot of foot traffic.

201
00:08:50,260 --> 00:08:51,730
That means it would've
been impossible to hide a body here.

202
00:08:52,440 --> 00:08:54,320
And a metal box this big...

203
00:08:54,480 --> 00:08:55,750
Could it have been moved here?

204
00:08:56,000 --> 00:08:57,630
Judging from the scene,

205
00:08:57,750 --> 00:08:58,960
the body must have been here

206
00:08:58,960 --> 00:09:00,150
for quite some time.

207
00:09:03,080 --> 00:09:04,600
Ma, flashlight.

208
00:09:06,790 --> 00:09:08,360
Can you make sense
of this, Officer Wang?

209
00:09:22,750 --> 00:09:24,840
Zhou, what's this?

210
00:09:25,870 --> 00:09:26,670
Charcoal.

211
00:09:26,870 --> 00:09:29,480
The body is severely dehydrated,

212
00:09:29,720 --> 00:09:31,440
dried out, and shriveled.

213
00:09:31,600 --> 00:09:32,910
That's how it ended up like this.

214
00:09:32,910 --> 00:09:33,840
So

215
00:09:33,960 --> 00:09:36,320
this could only happen in a dry,

216
00:09:36,320 --> 00:09:37,510
well-ventilated environment, right?

217
00:09:37,550 --> 00:09:38,510
Generally,

218
00:09:38,510 --> 00:09:41,390
when a body loses
40 percent of its moisture,

219
00:09:41,600 --> 00:09:43,440
bacterial growth is inhibited.

220
00:09:43,440 --> 00:09:45,120
Once it loses more than 50 percent,

221
00:09:45,150 --> 00:09:47,030
bacterial growth stops completely.

222
00:09:47,390 --> 00:09:48,910
If bacteria can no longer multiply,

223
00:09:48,910 --> 00:09:51,150
the body won't decompose.

224
00:09:51,670 --> 00:09:53,440
As the body continues to lose moisture,

225
00:09:53,790 --> 00:09:55,270
it will become a mummified body.

226
00:09:55,320 --> 00:09:57,480
But the climate here is so humid.

227
00:09:57,600 --> 00:09:58,910
It's even raining right now.

228
00:10:00,030 --> 00:10:02,360
How could the body become mummified?

229
00:10:03,960 --> 00:10:05,120
Take the body back

230
00:10:05,120 --> 00:10:05,960
for an autopsy.

231
00:10:05,960 --> 00:10:06,600
Okay.

232
00:10:10,000 --> 00:10:11,720
The body is severely mummified.

233
00:10:11,870 --> 00:10:13,240
The available evidence is insufficient.

234
00:10:13,790 --> 00:10:15,150
No usable fingerprints.

235
00:10:15,270 --> 00:10:17,000
No surveillance footage. No witnesses.

236
00:10:17,000 --> 00:10:18,510
After reviewing the case,

237
00:10:18,510 --> 00:10:20,600
all leads have been exhausted,
with no new developments.

238
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,320
The case is classified as a cold case.

239
00:10:24,670 --> 00:10:26,030
Longfan sure had

240
00:10:26,030 --> 00:10:27,030
a lot of unsolved cases in the '90s.

241
00:10:27,340 --> 00:10:28,960
(Mummy in the Rain Case)
Believe me.

242
00:10:29,200 --> 00:10:30,120
These unsolved cases

243
00:10:31,120 --> 00:10:32,480
really didn't exist before.

244
00:10:34,030 --> 00:10:35,000
It's because of my dad.

245
00:10:36,080 --> 00:10:36,870
Your dad?

246
00:10:38,030 --> 00:10:40,150
Didn't he die of stomach cancer?

247
00:10:41,320 --> 00:10:42,360
Then do you remember

248
00:10:42,510 --> 00:10:44,120
that before my dad
died of stomach cancer,

249
00:10:44,360 --> 00:10:45,750
he was also caught in a train explosion?

250
00:10:50,120 --> 00:10:51,000
Simply put,

251
00:10:51,550 --> 00:10:53,480
some supernatural things happened.

252
00:10:54,200 --> 00:10:55,720
I made contact with him

253
00:10:55,720 --> 00:10:56,790
while he was living in the '90s.

254
00:10:57,720 --> 00:10:59,240
He was originally
supposed to die in 1990,

255
00:10:59,750 --> 00:11:00,720
but I saved him.

256
00:11:01,240 --> 00:11:03,790
Later, he died of stomach cancer.

257
00:11:05,030 --> 00:11:06,630
What he means is

258
00:11:07,320 --> 00:11:10,720
he talked to his dad across time.

259
00:11:11,240 --> 00:11:12,750
I think that's what he means.

260
00:11:13,390 --> 00:11:14,790
Because I changed history,

261
00:11:14,840 --> 00:11:16,550
cases that originally never existed

262
00:11:16,960 --> 00:11:18,550
started happening one after another.

263
00:11:18,840 --> 00:11:20,600
This is what's known as

264
00:11:21,630 --> 00:11:22,670
the butterfly effect.

265
00:11:22,670 --> 00:11:23,550
You could say that.

266
00:11:23,550 --> 00:11:24,360
Anyway,

267
00:11:24,750 --> 00:11:26,600
this whole chain of cause
and effect started with me.

268
00:11:26,720 --> 00:11:27,510
Those people

269
00:11:29,480 --> 00:11:30,870
may have died because of me too.

270
00:11:30,870 --> 00:11:31,910
So you're saying

271
00:11:32,480 --> 00:11:34,910
my professional idol, Captain Qin,

272
00:11:35,030 --> 00:11:37,600
single-handedly
set three cases in motion.

273
00:11:37,790 --> 00:11:38,720
Comrade Qin Ming.

274
00:11:39,270 --> 00:11:41,030
Good thing we're in the 21st century

275
00:11:41,030 --> 00:11:42,910
and I've seen some sci-fi movies.

276
00:11:43,120 --> 00:11:44,480
Otherwise, I really
wouldn't understand this.

277
00:11:46,360 --> 00:11:48,320
I actually think it's pretty exciting.

278
00:11:48,790 --> 00:11:50,320
Wouldn't that mean we can

279
00:11:50,750 --> 00:11:52,270
hunt down criminals
across time from now on?

280
00:11:55,200 --> 00:11:56,000
So,

281
00:11:56,630 --> 00:11:57,960
you accept this explanation?

282
00:11:57,960 --> 00:11:58,670
Of course.

283
00:11:59,270 --> 00:12:00,600
Is it really that hard to understand?

284
00:12:01,080 --> 00:12:01,870
Is it?

285
00:12:01,870 --> 00:12:02,720
Not really.

286
00:12:03,670 --> 00:12:06,480
So as long as Captain Qin,
back in the '90s,

287
00:12:06,480 --> 00:12:07,790
finds the killer,

288
00:12:07,790 --> 00:12:08,790
everything that happened afterward

289
00:12:08,790 --> 00:12:09,790
won't happen.

290
00:12:09,790 --> 00:12:11,870
Exactly. The butterfly effect.

291
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:13,960
We just need to catch that butterfly.

292
00:12:14,080 --> 00:12:15,080
I refuse to believe

293
00:12:15,080 --> 00:12:17,240
two generations of police
working together can't catch him.

294
00:12:17,670 --> 00:12:18,480
Exactly.

295
00:12:20,320 --> 00:12:21,840
We just need to catch that butterfly.

296
00:12:30,000 --> 00:12:33,150
Should we talk him into seeing a doctor?

297
00:12:35,440 --> 00:12:38,000
You don't believe any of this?

298
00:12:38,030 --> 00:12:39,150
You do?

299
00:12:40,440 --> 00:12:41,600
He's Qin Ming.

300
00:12:41,600 --> 00:12:42,480
Of course I

301
00:12:44,670 --> 00:12:46,150
believe him a little.

302
00:12:48,120 --> 00:12:48,910
All right.

303
00:12:53,660 --> 00:13:01,820
(Longfan Urban Construction,
Give Us Back Our Hard-Earned Money)

304
00:13:01,840 --> 00:13:03,670
(Pay Us Back)
It's been blocked like this for a month.

305
00:13:03,960 --> 00:13:05,320
Liang Chao sure is keeping his cool.

306
00:13:06,390 --> 00:13:08,120
(Liang Chao, Fraudster)
He's not keeping his cool.

307
00:13:08,750 --> 00:13:10,120
He's keeping his head down.

308
00:13:10,910 --> 00:13:13,120
Li, have you found him?

309
00:13:13,440 --> 00:13:15,600
Captain Qin, not a chance.

310
00:13:16,000 --> 00:13:17,440
The victims
of the urban construction company

311
00:13:17,440 --> 00:13:18,320
and the employees who are owed wages

312
00:13:18,320 --> 00:13:19,840
have been blocking
this place for a month.

313
00:13:20,120 --> 00:13:21,910
They haven't even
seen a glimpse of Liang Chao.

314
00:13:21,960 --> 00:13:23,750
His phone is off, and no one's home.

315
00:13:23,960 --> 00:13:25,630
I've asked around everywhere.

316
00:13:25,790 --> 00:13:26,870
Everyone says they don't know.

317
00:13:28,030 --> 00:13:28,910
Something's not right.

318
00:13:30,030 --> 00:13:31,390
Captain Qin, what do you mean?

319
00:13:31,870 --> 00:13:34,150
He hasn't gone out
or shown his face for a month.

320
00:13:34,270 --> 00:13:36,270
Either he's hiding, or...

321
00:13:39,360 --> 00:13:42,000
Captain Qin, you mean

322
00:13:42,440 --> 00:13:43,360
Liang Chao...

323
00:13:43,720 --> 00:13:44,840
Don't jump to conclusions.

324
00:13:44,840 --> 00:13:47,360
Check when he was last seen.

325
00:13:47,870 --> 00:13:49,720
Let me know as soon
as you hear anything.

326
00:13:50,360 --> 00:13:51,150
Understood.

327
00:13:51,630 --> 00:13:52,840
I'll keep you updated.

328
00:14:06,640 --> 00:14:07,580
(Mummies and Mysterious Ancient Egypt)

329
00:14:07,580 --> 00:14:08,500
(Guide to Mummy Preservation)

330
00:14:09,030 --> 00:14:10,240
Something else happened.

331
00:14:10,750 --> 00:14:14,000
A mummified body was found
at a demolition site outside the city.

332
00:14:15,600 --> 00:14:16,910
Dad, I already know.

333
00:14:17,270 --> 00:14:18,790
There's another unsolved case file now.

334
00:14:19,150 --> 00:14:20,200
Mummy in the Rain.

335
00:14:23,390 --> 00:14:26,750
Do you think this
might be because of me again?

336
00:14:26,750 --> 00:14:27,390
Dad.

337
00:14:27,720 --> 00:14:29,390
Don't put the blame on yourself.

338
00:14:30,320 --> 00:14:31,200
This

339
00:14:32,120 --> 00:14:33,550
ultimately happened because of me.

340
00:14:35,200 --> 00:14:36,750
I'm the one who let that killer loose.

341
00:14:36,870 --> 00:14:37,670
But, Dad,

342
00:14:39,480 --> 00:14:40,390
I don't regret it.

343
00:14:41,320 --> 00:14:42,390
I still want to see

344
00:14:43,550 --> 00:14:44,840
if you'll be just
as charming when you're old

345
00:14:44,840 --> 00:14:46,000
as you are when you're young.

346
00:14:47,320 --> 00:14:49,910
Son, when it comes to comforting people,

347
00:14:50,120 --> 00:14:51,510
you're really not very good at it.

348
00:14:54,450 --> 00:14:55,390
But when it comes to solving cases,

349
00:14:55,390 --> 00:14:56,750
I'm definitely as good as you.

350
00:14:57,670 --> 00:14:59,120
Why do I find that so hard to believe?

351
00:15:00,840 --> 00:15:01,910
Have you been to the scene?

352
00:15:02,630 --> 00:15:03,440
Yeah.

353
00:15:03,840 --> 00:15:05,080
The body has already
dried and shriveled.

354
00:15:05,390 --> 00:15:06,840
The time of death can't be determined.

355
00:15:06,840 --> 00:15:08,550
There were no useful traces
at the scene either.

356
00:15:08,670 --> 00:15:10,080
The only thing we found was

357
00:15:11,080 --> 00:15:12,550
charcoal inside the metal box.

358
00:15:13,150 --> 00:15:13,960
Charcoal?

359
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:16,030
The case file didn't mention that.

360
00:15:16,750 --> 00:15:18,840
The charcoal,
together with the metal box,

361
00:15:18,910 --> 00:15:21,080
may have created the conditions
for the body to become mummified.

362
00:15:21,120 --> 00:15:22,320
So you mean

363
00:15:22,320 --> 00:15:24,320
the charcoal
was used to dry out the body?

364
00:15:24,790 --> 00:15:26,120
There are many
convenient small appliances now,

365
00:15:26,120 --> 00:15:28,870
such as ovens and air fryers.

366
00:15:29,000 --> 00:15:30,200
Air fryers in particular

367
00:15:30,200 --> 00:15:32,480
can quickly dehydrate food

368
00:15:32,550 --> 00:15:34,840
in a hot, dry environment.

369
00:15:35,750 --> 00:15:36,790
That metal box,

370
00:15:37,150 --> 00:15:38,510
if it was three months ago,

371
00:15:39,000 --> 00:15:40,270
when spring was turning into summer,

372
00:15:40,550 --> 00:15:42,510
the weather was still
hot, dry, and windy.

373
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:45,150
The temperature inside the metal box
would've been very high,

374
00:15:45,480 --> 00:15:47,720
like a small oven.

375
00:15:49,120 --> 00:15:50,630
Together with the charcoal inside,

376
00:15:51,000 --> 00:15:52,720
which is highly absorbent,

377
00:15:53,080 --> 00:15:54,600
it could quickly absorb the moisture

378
00:15:54,600 --> 00:15:55,840
evaporating from the body.

379
00:15:56,200 --> 00:15:57,390
With the two combined,

380
00:15:57,870 --> 00:15:59,750
it's entirely possible
that in a short time,

381
00:15:59,790 --> 00:16:01,270
the body could have become mummified.

382
00:16:02,720 --> 00:16:03,630
Just as you said,

383
00:16:03,630 --> 00:16:06,360
the weather three months ago
was indeed dry and hot.

384
00:16:06,870 --> 00:16:08,720
The body's facial features
are almost unrecognizable.

385
00:16:08,720 --> 00:16:10,390
If we want to identify the victim,

386
00:16:11,270 --> 00:16:12,080
we'll have to

387
00:16:13,390 --> 00:16:15,150
check the missing persons records.

388
00:16:44,600 --> 00:16:45,390
Qin Ming.

389
00:16:46,600 --> 00:16:47,390
Ming.

390
00:16:49,080 --> 00:16:49,870
Qin Ming.

391
00:16:51,080 --> 00:16:53,030
The victim was about 1.75 meters tall.

392
00:16:53,120 --> 00:16:54,000
Male.

393
00:16:54,960 --> 00:16:55,870
Look here.

394
00:16:55,870 --> 00:16:58,360
There's a slight, roughly
circular depression in the bone.

395
00:16:58,360 --> 00:16:59,440
The shape

396
00:17:00,240 --> 00:17:03,320
looks like it was caused by a blow
from something like a hammer.

397
00:17:03,390 --> 00:17:04,200
A hammer?

398
00:17:04,880 --> 00:17:05,830
A hammer again?

399
00:17:05,960 --> 00:17:06,830
But Huo Qicheng...

400
00:17:06,830 --> 00:17:07,830
Let me finish.

401
00:17:08,070 --> 00:17:09,270
This injury wasn't fatal.

402
00:17:09,350 --> 00:17:11,400
It only affected
the outer table of the skull.

403
00:17:11,680 --> 00:17:12,960
The inner table wasn't affected,

404
00:17:13,310 --> 00:17:15,590
so there was no damage to the brainstem

405
00:17:15,680 --> 00:17:16,640
or vital centers.

406
00:17:16,750 --> 00:17:18,590
It seems more like the blow
was meant to subdue him instantly

407
00:17:18,790 --> 00:17:20,640
and stop him from resisting.

408
00:17:20,640 --> 00:17:21,480
Knock him unconscious first,

409
00:17:22,070 --> 00:17:23,830
then kill him some other way.

410
00:17:23,830 --> 00:17:25,750
The mucous membranes of the mouth
and nose are completely destroyed.

411
00:17:26,000 --> 00:17:28,110
The skin on the neck
has also shriveled up.

412
00:17:28,350 --> 00:17:30,160
Even if there were signs
of pressure around the neck,

413
00:17:30,200 --> 00:17:31,200
they can no longer be seen.

414
00:17:31,400 --> 00:17:34,110
Combined with
the nonfatal blow to the skull,

415
00:17:34,310 --> 00:17:36,790
I think the cause of death
may have been asphyxia.

416
00:17:37,590 --> 00:17:38,400
Of course,

417
00:17:38,400 --> 00:17:40,750
we still need
to find physical signs of asphyxia.

418
00:17:41,200 --> 00:17:43,510
What about the cause
of death? His identity?

419
00:17:44,310 --> 00:17:45,550
Could this end up
as a case with no leads?

420
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:47,240
The body has dried out this badly.

421
00:17:47,240 --> 00:17:48,960
None of the usual methods will work.

422
00:17:49,750 --> 00:17:51,310
As for who he is,

423
00:17:53,000 --> 00:17:54,350
I do have a way

424
00:17:54,440 --> 00:17:55,440
we can try.

425
00:17:55,440 --> 00:17:57,060
(Mummy)

426
00:18:00,960 --> 00:18:02,480
How is it? Can you reconstruct his face?

427
00:18:03,270 --> 00:18:05,550
We only have a photo of the victim,
and it's of a mummified body.

428
00:18:05,750 --> 00:18:06,790
The skull wasn't preserved,

429
00:18:06,790 --> 00:18:07,960
and there are no CT scan records.

430
00:18:08,550 --> 00:18:09,720
We can't do a facial reconstruction.

431
00:18:09,720 --> 00:18:11,070
Let's enhance the image first.

432
00:18:12,880 --> 00:18:14,400
The algorithm
can only improve the clarity.

433
00:18:14,510 --> 00:18:16,640
It can't correct the soft tissue
distortion caused by mummification.

434
00:18:43,270 --> 00:18:44,310
Who is this supposed to be?

435
00:18:44,310 --> 00:18:45,030
Come on, Qin.

436
00:18:45,030 --> 00:18:46,680
Why do you have to be so harsh?

437
00:18:46,880 --> 00:18:48,550
I've only learned the basics myself.

438
00:18:48,550 --> 00:18:50,790
Of course I can't compare
with the experts at the provincial department.

439
00:18:51,240 --> 00:18:53,160
I'm mainly going for speed here.

440
00:18:54,750 --> 00:18:55,720
Zhou.

441
00:18:56,070 --> 00:18:58,270
You've really only learned the basics.

442
00:18:58,920 --> 00:19:00,830
At least give him
some recognizable features.

443
00:19:02,070 --> 00:19:03,030
I'll try again.

444
00:19:05,400 --> 00:19:07,310
After a mummified body
becomes dehydrated and shrinks,

445
00:19:07,830 --> 00:19:09,240
the entire face contracts inward.

446
00:19:09,400 --> 00:19:11,350
The eyes narrow, the nostrils collapse,

447
00:19:11,830 --> 00:19:12,880
and the lips recede.

448
00:19:28,440 --> 00:19:30,480
Raise the brow ridge a little.

449
00:19:32,240 --> 00:19:34,240
Narrow the nasal bone a little more.

450
00:19:34,480 --> 00:19:35,350
About two millimeters.

451
00:19:41,000 --> 00:19:42,960
That's pretty good, actually.

452
00:19:44,350 --> 00:19:45,310
Hey, remember

453
00:19:45,310 --> 00:19:47,310
that Indian movie
we watched a while back?

454
00:19:47,880 --> 00:19:49,880
Doesn't he look like the male lead?

455
00:19:50,920 --> 00:19:52,070
The really handsome one.

456
00:19:53,000 --> 00:19:54,920
The skinny guy with the thin face.

457
00:19:55,510 --> 00:19:56,720
Remember the song?

458
00:20:01,510 --> 00:20:02,270
And his eyes...

459
00:20:02,960 --> 00:20:03,880
That look he did.

460
00:20:03,880 --> 00:20:04,640
Remember?

461
00:20:14,200 --> 00:20:16,070
Awaara. I know.

462
00:20:16,160 --> 00:20:16,960
Right, right.

463
00:20:17,270 --> 00:20:18,680
I fell asleep during it.

464
00:20:19,240 --> 00:20:22,000
Looks great.
I just can't tell who it is.

465
00:20:26,400 --> 00:20:27,200
It's him.

466
00:20:30,320 --> 00:20:34,840
♪The old walkie-talkie I treasure♪

467
00:20:37,910 --> 00:20:42,690
♪The birthday surprise
you gave me that year♪

468
00:20:45,400 --> 00:20:50,780
♪Its buttons worn
and weathered with time♪

469
00:20:51,310 --> 00:20:56,640
♪Still echoing your words,
"Be brave and keep moving on"♪

470
00:20:58,670 --> 00:21:06,630
♪The old train rolled over
our reluctance to part♪

471
00:21:07,260 --> 00:21:12,310
♪You waved goodbye
and faded into the night♪

472
00:21:14,350 --> 00:21:22,660
♪I used to think
we'd always have more time♪

473
00:21:22,660 --> 00:21:28,510
♪But that goodbye became the last♪

474
00:21:29,970 --> 00:21:38,090
♪I carry the warmth you left behind♪

475
00:21:38,780 --> 00:21:43,820
♪Making my way
through every door in life♪

476
00:21:45,600 --> 00:21:53,640
♪Whenever a train
whistle sounds at night♪

477
00:21:53,920 --> 00:22:01,190
♪I suddenly long to call out to you♪

478
00:22:01,390 --> 00:22:05,800
♪Can you hear me?♪

479
00:22:05,810 --> 00:22:09,600
♪Can you hear me?♪

480
00:22:09,600 --> 00:22:17,060
♪Let the old receiver
carry the words I never said♪

481
00:22:17,060 --> 00:22:24,800
♪I've taken on
both your duty and your love♪

482
00:22:25,130 --> 00:22:30,740
♪This train has no return, and when I
look back, you're no longer waiting♪

483
00:22:32,620 --> 00:22:36,220
♪After all these years♪

484
00:22:38,730 --> 00:22:46,210
♪How I wish I could
talk to you just one more time♪

485
00:22:47,110 --> 00:22:48,410
♪And tell you♪

486
00:22:49,630 --> 00:22:52,900
♪I haven't let you down♪
